     recognized ModellingRule no prior e2e scenario uses (all others use
     plain Optional/Mandatory, NodeId 80/78), combined with an explicit
     ValueRank=3 array (3 dimensions, collapsing into the same
     ValueRank_MoreDimensions symbolic leaf as ValueRank=2 does in
     test_vt_contradiction.NodeSet2, auditing that collapsing at a
     different concrete rank).

     DeviceType declares a MandatoryPlaceholder Variable "Channel" :
     PropertyType/Double, ValueRank=3. get_modelling_rule maps
     MandatoryPlaceholder to (is_optional=False, is_placeholder=True): the
     same cardinality treatment as plain Mandatory (a
     minQualifiedCardinality(1) restriction, since instances still must
     provide at least one actual node under this placeholder), on top of
     the array ValueRank handling. Expect DeviceType's own Virtual Type for
     "Channel" to be subClassOf PropertyType, ValueRank_MoreDimensions, and
     a Double Datatype restriction, with both allValuesFrom and
     minQualifiedCardinality(1) written on DeviceType itself. No
     contradiction expected: this just confirms the placeholder and array
     mechanisms compose correctly together. -->
